IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc19-s492-25.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, s 492.25 Notice to Victims (text lines 10975-10983), in PART XV.1 Unreasonable Delay.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Subsections (1) to (3) are duties of the prosecutor and of the court; subsection (4) says the prosecutor's failure does not stop the court deciding.
-- Each duty is encoded twice, as a decision function over the facts (MAYBE BOOLEAN) and as a regulative rule (DEONTIC), which is exercised with #TRACE.
-- "as soon as feasible" is the text's own measure; it gives no number of days, so the regulative rules carry no WITHIN (a period would be invented; fork F14).
-- JUST FALSE: a failed "if" or "after" of a duty is the text's no (rule of 2026-10-29 (a); listed in NOTES.md, Marginal readings). NOTHING: not covered.
-- SEAM: "victim" is a section 2 term. Whether there is a victim is taken as an INPUT named for the section it comes from, `s 2 victim: ...`, typed MAYBE BOOLEAN as the keel's `s 2 victim` answers
-- (its extension "for the purposes of sections 672.5, 722 and 745.63" leaves other purposes NOT COVERED); a NOTHING from it is carried through, never turned into FALSE.

§ `s 492.25(1) -- reasonable steps to inform any victim of the filing of the application`

-- "If an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court, the prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible, take reasonable steps to inform any victim of the offence
-- referred to in the application of the filing of the application." The duty arises when the application is filed ("If": a failed "if" is JUST FALSE). "any victim" is a scope: with no victim
-- there is no one to inform, and the text does not say what then follows: NOTHING (scope limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c); fork F4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:10977 | 492.25 (1) If an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court, the prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible, take reasonable steps to inform any victim of the offence referred to in the application of the filing of the application.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(1) (src:10977)
GIVEN `an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: there is a victim of the offence referred to in the application` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.25(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 victim: there is a victim of the offence referred to in the application`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any victim of the offence referred to in the application"
         WHEN JUST victim THEN
             IF victim
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any victim of the offence referred to in the application"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(1) (src:10977)
DECLARE `s 492.25(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.25(1) take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing of the application`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. A NOTHING from the decision function states no duty, so the rule is FULFILLED (nothing owed on the text).
@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(1) (src:10977)
GIVEN `an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: there is a victim of the offence referred to in the application` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.25(1) act`
`s 492.25(1) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the filing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 492.25(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing` `an application for a finding of unreasonable delay is filed with the court` `s 2 victim: there is a victim of the offence referred to in the application`
    WHEN JUST owed THEN
        IF owed
        THEN PARTY `the prosecutor`
             MUST `s 492.25(1) take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the filing of the application`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the prosecutor` BECAUSE "s 492.25(1): reasonable steps were not taken to inform the victims of the filing of the application"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

§ `s 492.25(2) -- the court to inquire whether notice was given`

-- "The court shall, at the time the application is heard, inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims, if any, of the filing of the application."
-- The duty is on the court, at the time the application is heard ("at the time": a time the text fixes in its own words, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE: "at the time" is read as "when", which counts as "where", and a failed "where" is JUST FALSE, rulings of 2026-11-05; fork F13).
-- ", if any" qualifies the victims inquired about, not the duty, so the existence of a victim is not a gate here.
-- src:10979 | (2) The court shall, at the time the application is heard, inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims, if any, of the filing of the application.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(2) (src:10979)
GIVEN `the application for a finding of unreasonable delay is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.25(2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims` MEANS
    IF `the application for a finding of unreasonable delay is being heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time the application is heard"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(2) (src:10979)
DECLARE `s 492.25(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.25(2) inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the filing of the application`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(2) (src:10979)
GIVEN `the application for a finding of unreasonable delay is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.25(2) act`
`s 492.25(2) the duty of the court to inquire of the prosecutor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 492.25(2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims` `the application for a finding of unreasonable delay is being heard`
    WHEN JUST owed THEN
        IF owed
        THEN PARTY `the court`
             MUST `s 492.25(2) inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the filing of the application`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 492.25(2): the court did not inquire of the prosecutor, at the time the application was heard, whether reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

§ `s 492.25(3) -- notice of the court's decision`

-- "The prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible after a decision has been made on the application, take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the decision."
-- Two gates, each in the text's own words: "after a decision has been made on the application" and "the victims, if any" (a failed "if": JUST FALSE).
-- src:10981 | (3) The prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible after a decision has been made on the application, take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(3) (src:10981)
GIVEN `a decision has been made on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: there are victims of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.25(3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a decision has been made on the application`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after a decision has been made on the application"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 victim: there are victims of the offence`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the victims, if any"
         WHEN JUST victims THEN
             IF victims
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the victims, if any"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(3) (src:10981)
DECLARE `s 492.25(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.25(3) take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision on the application`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(3) (src:10981)
GIVEN `a decision has been made on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: there are victims of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.25(3) act`
`s 492.25(3) the duty of the prosecutor to inform the victims of the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 492.25(3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision` `a decision has been made on the application` `s 2 victim: there are victims of the offence`
    WHEN JUST owed THEN
        IF owed
        THEN PARTY `the prosecutor`
             MUST `s 492.25(3) take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the decision on the application`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the prosecutor` BECAUSE "s 492.25(3): reasonable steps were not taken to inform the victims of the decision on the application"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

§ `s 492.25(4) -- a failure to inform does not preclude the decision`

-- "The failure of the prosecutor to take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the application does not preclude the court from making a decision in respect of the application."
-- A flat negative (N2: it counts as the text's no). The function is named for the preclusion: JUST FALSE = the failure does not preclude the court from deciding.
-- Where there was no such failure the section does not speak (it is about that failure only): NOTHING. A failure to inform the victims of the DECISION (subsection (3)) is not this failure.
-- src:10983 | (4) The failure of the prosecutor to take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the application does not preclude the court from making a decision in respect of the application.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.25(4) (src:10983)
GIVEN `the prosecutor failed to take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.25(4) the failure of the prosecutor precludes the court from making a decision on the application` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor failed to take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the application`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not preclude the court from making a decision in respect of the application"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The failure of the prosecutor to take reasonable steps to inform the victims, if any, of the application"
